  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Harishankar Rampravesh Singh vs State Of Maharashtra on 7 June, 2024 P.H. Jayani 03 aba1518.2024.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1518 Of 2024 Harishankar Rampravesh Singh .... Applicant V/s. The State of Maharashtra .... Respondent Mr. Nehal Desale for the Applicant. Mr. Mayur Sonavane, App for the State. Ms. Sneha Solanke, Psi, Uttan Sagari Police Station, present. Coram: Shyam C. Chandak, J. Dated : 07th June, 2024.",
    "facts": "Learned APP submitted that, at the relevant time the main accused namely Salman Idris Khan was found in possession of the contraband (gutkha). On inquiry, he disclosed that, it was procured by his brother/co-accused Naushad Khan from the present Applicant. As such, there is a prima facie case of a serious offence against the Applicant. The offence is of the year 2021. Learned Advocate for the Applicant made a statement that, the arrest of the co-accused Naushad Khan was stayed by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in April, 2022 and produced the said Order dated 01st April, 2022. The alleged contraband (gutkha) is already seized.",
    "arguments": "3) Learned Advocate for the Applicant submitted that, neither the Applicant is figured in the FIR nor the investigating material transpired his role in the alleged crime. Thus, the Applicant is not directly or indirectly involved in the offence. Therefore, ad-interim protection may be granted to the Applicant.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3) Learned Advocate for the Applicant submitted that, neither the Applicant is figured in the FIR nor the investigating material transpired his role in the alleged crime. Thus, the Applicant is not directly or indirectly involved in the offence. Therefore, ad-interim protection may be granted to the Applicant.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
